# issue: none
# notes: A ranked scan reads only the columns its query needs: `return { $d.slug }` under a
# notes: `nearest` or `bm25` order reads the id and the key alone, and a bare `$d` reads the node's
# notes: returned scalar properties but not the unreturned `embedding`. Sixty docs alternate
# notes: "alpha doc" / "beta doc" titles, doc n sits at distance n from the origin, and every
# notes: alpha doc ties on BM25 score, so the bm25 step's ten rows are the id tie-break's
# notes: first ten alpha docs. Replaces the Rust test
# notes: search_scans_project_needed_columns_and_the_scoring_column (search.rs); its
# notes: `node_scan_projections` probe is the `columns` plan line here (the v2 scan projection
# notes: does not list the `_distance`/`_score` column the retrieval appends), and its "no gate
# notes: verdict" assertion has no v2 plan or row form.

--- runner
timeout_ms: 10000
environments:
  - target: omnigraph-engine
    storage: local-filesystem

--- schema
node Doc {
    slug: String @key
    title: String @index
    embedding: Vector(4) @index
}

--- seed
{"type":"Doc","data":{"slug":"n00000","title":"alpha doc","embedding":[0.0,0.0,0.0,0.0]}}
